{"The 'next' pagination action allows offset to become exactly user_count, which will request an empty page of members - offset should be capped to the start of the last page (max(user_count - limit, 0))": 0.7199708223342896, "totalPages uses Math.floor(user_count / limit) + 1, which creates an extra page whenever user_count is an exact multiple of limit (e.g. 100/50 => 3), making pagination UI incorrect": 0.8932202458381653, "findMembers returns 'return ;' when the group has no name, which returns undefined and can break call sites that expect a promise": 0.7026633620262146, "group.visible is always overwritten based on params, so requests that omit visible will unintentionally set it to false": 0.8709237575531006, "name isn't stripped on update (unlike create), allowing leading/trailing whitespace through": 0.8490001559257507, "Splitting usernames without stripping/deduping can fail to add users when there are spaces (e.g. 'bob, sam')": 0.8945356011390686, "Splitting usernames without deduping can raise a unique constraint error when adding existing members (group_users has a unique index on [group_id,user_id])": 0.695889949798584, "group.add persists via the association, so the later group.save is redundant and can report failure after members were already added": 0.512759804725647, "Using group.users.delete(user_id) removes the join row without destroy callbacks, so the GroupUser counter cache (groups.user_count) won't be updated and membership side-effects can be skipped": 0.9023706316947937, "The subsequent group.save isn't needed for join-table removal": 0.27627643942832947, "The group_member template references member and automatic, but the corresponding view doesn't define those bindings - in Ember list item views the item is typically available as content/context, so this will render blanks": 0.7272816300392151, "The group_member template will always show the remove link for automatic groups since automatic will be undefined": 0.8676474094390869}